Subject: winedmo: announce H.264 coded output size to the reader
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Modification date: 2026-11-07

H.264 streams are commonly coded at a macroblock-aligned size larger than
the visible frame (e.g. 1920x1088 storage for 1920x1080 content). The decoder
output type only carries the negotiated visible size, so when the real output
differs, signal a one-shot format change carrying the coded-size type (with
the visible apertures). Without this, the downstream converter converts only
the visible aperture and misplaces the chroma planes, painting the leading
padding rows bright green.

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
index 0d6c14f..1ab0342 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -1401,6 +1474,22 @@ NTSTATUS transform_get_output( void *arg )
                 return STATUS_SUCCESS;
             }
         }
+
+        /* Decoders may output the coded size (e.g. 1088 for 1080 H.264) while
+         * the negotiated output type only carries the visible size. Signal a
+         * format change once so the caller picks up the coded-size type with
+         * the visible apertures; out_width/out_height track what was announced
+         * to avoid signalling repeatedly. */
+        if (!t->is_raw_video && t->out_width > 0 && t->out_height > 0
+                && should_use_coded_video_output_size( t, width, height )
+                && (t->out_width != t->avctx->coded_width || t->out_height != t->avctx->coded_height))
+        {
+            t->out_width = t->avctx->coded_width;
+            t->out_height = t->avctx->coded_height;
+            params->flags |= WINEDMO_SAMPLE_FLAG_FORMAT_CHANGED;
+            params->size   = 0;
+            return STATUS_SUCCESS; /* frame_pending stays true */
+        }
     }
 
     /* ---- Output the frame ---- */
